Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-arm.c
Line: 1810
Function: bfd_arm_allocate_interworking_sections
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: The result of bfd_alloc(...) is not checked for NULL before assigning to s->contents. If allocation fails, s->contents remains NULL but later code writes into s->contents (e.g., bfd_put_16/32 at lines 1505-1510 and 1526-1529), leading to a NULL pointer dereference.

